## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical testing of dynamic feature flags and edge propagation, race conditions, and rollback paths under real-world latency. It requires concrete test design, tooling, and observability considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant feature flags and canary
- Edge propagation latency and cache invalidation
- Race condition testing during toggles
- Rollback and observability (metrics/logs)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test sketch
test('canary flag propagation across edge', async () => {
  setFlag('TenantA','newContent',true);
  await wait(35000);
  const rA = await httpGet('/content?tenant=TenantA', headers);
  const rB = await httpGet('/content?tenant=TenantB', headers);
  expect(rA.flag).toBe(true);
  expect(rB.flag).toBe(false);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you automate clock manipulation in test env to simulate propagation windows?
- How would you measure edge propagation latency and flag consistency across regions?
